how to do that.  So I should have just one top-level, with only thing using
=SUBDIRS= being gnulib.

** TODO Document updating the web page

- The CVS repository can be checked out using:

  #+begin_src sh
    cd /tmp
    guix shell -E CVS_RSH=ssh cvs \
         -- cvs -z3 -d:ext:gray_wolf@cvs.savannah.gnu.org:/web/gengetopt co gengetopt
  #+end_src
- Both [[file:doc/gengetopt.html][manual]] and [[file:doc/index.html][index]] are generated during build, so copy them over into the
  CVS repository.
- And finally commit the changes:

  #+begin_src sh
    guix shell -E CVS_RSH=ssh cvs \
         -- cvs -z3 -d:ext:gray_wolf@cvs.savannah.gnu.org:/web/gengetopt commit gengetopt.html index.html
  #+end_src
- It takes some time (~5 minutes?) for the changes to appear live.
